# PR merge workflow

When asked to merge, merge yourself. Do not ask the user to click Merge.

**Working path** (Cursor GitHub App via Shell `gh`):

```bash
gh api -X PUT repos/momijineko/fanqie-web-reader/pulls/<N>/merge \
  -f merge_method=squash \
  -f commit_title='<title> (#<N>)' \
  -f sha=<head_sha>
```

If conversations block merge: resolve threads first, wait for required CI, retry the normal merge. Do **not** use `gh pr merge --admin` unless the user explicitly asks to bypass branch protection.

**Do not use for merge:**

- `Github.merge_pull_request` MCP → always 403 with user PAT
- `ManagePullRequest` → no merge action
- Direct push to `main` → branch protection
- `gh pr merge --admin` as a default fallback → bypasses required checks

“用 Cursor 的 / 不要用 gh” means use the App `gh` token (`gh auth status` → account `cursor`), not “refuse to merge”.
